    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Brice Turang**, **James Wood**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Tyler Soderstrom** form the core of our lineup, all clearing the 72-point threshold as our most efficient starts. **James Wood** leads the group with a 75.37 rating, fueled by an elite 0.422 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Ritchie. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) are massive beneficiaries of park factors today, with both seeing a +10% to +14% boost to their base projections. We are leaning heavily into these high-efficiency spots to bolster our Roto standing, prioritizing their ability to capitalize on shaky opposing arms like Montero and Lugo while maintaining high-leverage spots in the order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal slot occupied by **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly edged out **Austin Riley** (46.04) and **Cole Young** (43.76). While **Austin Riley** boasts a higher pedigree, his lower projectable floor against Cavalli and a suboptimal #8 spot in the order kept him on the bench in favor of **Zach McKinstry**\u2019s park-adjusted utility. We remain wary of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll**, both of whom are facing the elite arm of Williams (2.99 xERA). Despite their talent, the matchup drag on their scores\u2014coupled with an elite catcher warning for **Corbin Carroll**\u2014suggests a lower ceiling than their standard output. We will continue to monitor the weather and official lineups for any late-breaking shifts that might force us to pivot from these current projections.",
